  "scenario": {
    "summary": "Guest opens the registration page from Sign In, checks its heading, goes back to Sign In, ticks Remember Me, signs in with the class account, logs off and checks the username is remembered.",
    "steps": [
      "Open the webstore, click Login",
      "Click Create Account, verify 'REGISTER FOR AN ACCOUNT'",
      "Click Login Now",
      "Tick Remember Me, sign in with the sheet account",
      "Log off",
      "Verify the username field is pre-filled with the account username"
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "user"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "Signs in and logs off; Remember Me cookie set in the browser"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "Registration heading",
      "Username remembered"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "DECLARED ACCOUNT (per method): the method signs in with the sheet account testClassRetailUsers/loginTest (loginAndRegistration!B172/C172). Convention: every method that signs in declares user = USER_WEBSTORE_REGISTERED {store}, preferred {source: the username source, required: true} (Tda.declareUser -> useExisting). Username/password stay credential sources (masked).",
      "verifyRememberMe compares the pre-filled username with the same credential source (the declared account's username).",
      "Store: openWebstoreUrl opens automation_webStoreUrl (atstage: webstore-z10-atstage, the main store MaxwellsHardware), the same store as the Selenium pdp/quickOrder/plp entries.",
      "Profile: work/profiles/profile.json has no observations for these Selenium cells (profiled false); DB facts from bin/tda rows (2026-11-11) where cited.",
      "Scanned constant values (locators, report messages, map keys, image paths) are framework constants: role config, no need.",
      "migrate: Selenium reads Excel tables through TestData.getMap / getHashMap; there is no swap for Selenium."
    ],
    "confidence": "high",
    "needsReview": false
  },
